Resolved audit findings (2026-10-18; reviewed HEAD 2793ef4):
Report: doc/reviews/review-followup-2026-10-18.txt; observed fixture results in .json.
- [FIXED] A1: Shared finite/positive/invertible gain-scale validation and an
    apply-pass check prevent infinite Wave64 Undo scales. Retain its upper bound.
- [FIXED] A2: Windows -e allocates checked command lengths, validates Win32
    path lengths, and refuses shell-limit overflow before processing audio.
    Command environment filenames are dynamically allocated.
- [FIXED] A3: Invocation-wide input identity/path tracking rejects duplicates
    before each batch, including aliases of the original and replaced file.
- [FIXED] A4: Validate effective PCM length against frame size before deriving
    bounded frame counts; RIFF padding and valid odd mono 8-bit input still work.
- [FIXED] A5: Album and Windows command DC display use truncated double values
    without narrowing to int, including large finite float input and log output.
- [FIXED] A6: Extensible WAV/Wave64 validate extension length and precision;
    valid left-aligned PCM and unspecified legacy precision remain supported.
