and test/command_regressions.c. Details: doc/reviews/review-followup-fixes-2026-10-18.txt.

Stereo analysis follow-up (2026-10-18; base 8a9a9f7):
- [IMPLEMENTED] AArch64 paired IIR histories and immediate second-stage
    filtering retain scalar arithmetic and complete planar output histories.
    Other targets retain the former paired implementation by default.
    Local peak/DC accumulators preserve summation order; extended-evaluation
    targets retain volatile binary64 DC rounding points.
    See doc/performance/stereo-optimization.txt and doc/performance/stereo-performance-windows.json.
- [OPEN] Native GCC/MSVC, hardware x64, x87, macOS/Linux and real-music
    throughput validation. Investigate x64 filter register pressure before
    enabling the full-history implementation on that architecture.

Exact mono filter reuse (2026-10-17; base 31cf06a):
- [IMPLEMENTED] Compute identical mono IIR channel filters once and mirror
    output histories; disable reuse after stereo until an analysis reset.
    All-rate mixed-channel state probes, ARM64/x64 gates, UBSan, and 1,260
    complete audio-file comparisons pass. Mono analysis is ~1.75x faster
    on Windows ARM64 (O2 and O3/ThinLTO); stereo speed is essentially unchanged.
    Additional mono RMS reuse did not help and was removed. Measurements and
    platform limits: doc/performance/mono-optimization.txt, mono-performance-windows.json.
- [OPEN] Confirm on native MSVC/GCC, macOS/Linux and hardware x64; measure
    long real-music mono recordings and default release flags on those targets.

Windows directory quality follow-up (2026-10-17; base c1f6d79):
- [FIXED] Recursive junction/symlink cycles and unintended external directory
    traversal. Cloud reparse points are distinguished from directory redirects;
