    tests are part of the gate. See doc/reviews/windows-directory-quality.txt.
- [OPEN] Real SMB/cloud-provider, case-sensitive NTFS and native POSIX checks.

Verified PCM optimization follow-up (2026-10-17; base 44db4a7):
- [IMPLEMENTED] Specialized no-dither/no-limiter integer gain application,
    preserving half-LSB rounding, DC and the legacy symmetric 32-bit clamp.
    Kernel oracles, UBSan and 1,260 prior/current output comparisons pass.
    Direct planar output packing was measured and rejected (no speed gain).
- [FIXED] Windows directory diagnostics preserve GetLastError before printing,
    treat system messages as data, and fall back safely if formatting fails.
    Fault injection covers these cases. Avoid MinGW argc/argv macro collisions
    in getopt declarations and one-past-end channel-stride pointer formation.
- [IMPLEMENTED] Exact integer PCM decode specialization and mirrored high-rate
    FIR history with bitwise oracles; configurable release optimization/LTO;
    ReplayGain and loudness verification use the actual linker flags.
    See doc/performance/pcm-optimization.txt and doc/performance/pcm-performance-windows.json.
- [IMPLEMENTED] Native Windows gate runner, prior/current complete output
    comparison (now 1,260 conditions), and portable warm-cache benchmark tooling.
- [FIXED] Windows x64 binary64 subnormal gain-metadata serialization; expanded
    positive/negative subnormal and signed-zero regression coverage.
- [OPEN] Native GCC/MSVC and macOS/Linux verification of these changes;
    official EBU signal conformance and sustained real-music measurements.
    File-level parallelism still requires the state encapsulation listed below.

