Implementation follow-up: 2026-10-14 (base commit 8b224d3).
Details: doc/reviews/todo-fixes.txt
Historical investigation: doc/reviews/todo-investigation.txt / .json
Current probe results: doc/reviews/todo-fixed.json
Reproduce: make check; make check-interop (requires FFmpeg)

- [DONE] Native 64-bit audio corruption / forced -m32 build.
    Fixed in 8b224d3: fixed-width PCM, portable lrint, native builds,
    large-file offsets and fast-mode positions. PCM and large-file checks
    cover the fix, including sparse Wave64 input/output above 4 GiB.

- [DONE] Percentages sometimes show > 100% done (or inf%).
    Progress uses processed frames per file and planned per-file durations
    overall. Short/fractional durations, mixed sample rates, skipped files,
    Undo and empty audio are covered. Successful writes finish at 100%.

- [DONE] ReplayGain / manual gain / DC correction / clipping.
    Channel extrema and actual frame counts determine peaks after the
    selected track/album DC correction. Gain caps use corrected peaks;
    album caps are selected after all track means are known. Manual gain
    is added once. The limiter retains its existing cap unless --noclip
    is used. New Peak is documented as the pre-limiter prediction.
    Regression coverage includes asymmetric PCM/float, distinct album
    means, manual gain, no-offset, limiter and unshaped dither.

- [DONE] --help layout, wildcard instructions, man/HTML sync.
    doc/help.json generates CLI text, README help, nroff and HTML via
    make docs. make check-docs rejects stale files and undocumented options.
    Build/platform conditions, Wave64, byte-based fast thresholds, quoting,
    case sensitivity and peak/limiter semantics are retained or clarified.
    Runtime checks covered macOS arm64/x86_64 and Linux x86_64; a MinGW-w64
    build was checked under Wine. Later Windows ARM64 native and emulated x64
    runs are recorded above; MSVC and hardware x64 remain follow-ups.
- [OPEN] The 'gain' chunk scale is big-endian on macOS (__APPLE__) and
    little-endian elsewhere, so -w files are not portable across them.

- [OPEN] Standard license/copyright headers in all sources.
    Deferred to a separate change: source license notices are unchanged
    here. Findings are in doc/reviews/todo-investigation.txt.

Performance investigation (2026-10-14): doc/performance/conversion-performance.txt
- [DONE] Paired stereo ReplayGain filters: expression-preserving SIMD on
    Clang and GCC 5+ for AArch64 and x86_64, with FP contraction disabled in
    the filters so scalar and paired paths are bitwise identical.
    Mono and other targets retain scalar/legacy paths.
    Use make verified-release (VERIFY_SIMD=auto|1|0) to require runtime
    equality before installation.
    Kernel/API state, histogram boundaries and unaffected-rate output
    match the scalar reference bit-for-bit on tested builds. Current benchmark
    gives ~1.5x ordinary stereo conversion throughput on macOS arm64.
    Details and limits: doc/performance/filter-simd-investigation.txt.
- [DONE] IEEE float serializer: replace frexp/byte reconstruction with guarded
    binary32 bit copying and an explicit little-endian fallback. Subnormals
    retain their value; signed zeros still serialize as positive zero.
    Exact-byte edge tests and input immutability checks cover the serializer.
- [DONE] 88.2kHz ReplayGain: both old denominators were unstable (real poles
    ~1.426 and ~1.067). Replace only this rate with FFmpeg coefficients in both
    table layouts; all twelve rates pass stability checks. Reject non-finite
    RMS levels and clamp before histogram casts. FFmpeg comparison and
    mono/stereo WAV/Wave64 conversion/undo checks cover the corrected rate.
- [DONE] Legacy SSE2 Yule kernel used padding instead of b10. Correct its
    final numerator tap; all-rate impulse/DC/tone checks against long-double
    reference pass under x86_64 Clang, including Windows x64 emulation.
    Native MSVC and hardware x64 remain platform validation follow-ups.
- [DONE] Reuse conversion/packing buffers per output file; check allocation,
    byte-count overflow and write failures before replacing the original file.
    Buffer reuse preserves integer packing and gain/dither/RNG arithmetic.
    See doc/performance/conversion-safe-implementation.txt and conversion-safe-performance.json.
    Overall speed differences remain small in the 96 kHz synthetic benchmark.
- [OPEN] Profile noise-shaped dither and common-path specialization separately;
    preserve RNG/history/rounding semantics. Compiler flags alone gave only
    modest or inconsistent gains in this workload.
